<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>FL2025_Exam 44</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; }
h1 { color: #C0392B; font-size: 20pt; }
h2 { color: #1F618D; font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 24px; }
.qtext { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
.opt { margin: 4px 0 4px 20px; }
.correct { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedwrong { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedright { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.explain { background: #F4F6F6; padding: 8px; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }
.video { margin-top:6px; }
img { max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; display:block; }
</style></head><body><h1>FL2025_EXAM 44 - Ket qua &amp; giai thich</h1><p><b>Ho ten:</b> Hang Tran<br/><b>Ket qua:</b> 3/28<br/><b>Thoi gian lam bai:</b> 48 giây<br/><b>Nop bai:</b> 2026-08-03T07:37:19.776Z</p><hr/><h2>Cau hoi 1</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is an example of shift-right testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Static code analysis [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Usability testing befor release</div><div class="opt correct">c. A/B testing in production [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Unit testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Tra glossary khái niệm "shift-right testing -A test approach to test a system continuously in production" là test ở production nên chọn C, A/B testing là test ngẫu nhiên với 1 số lượng user trên môi trường thật để đánh giá xem phần thay đổi của hệ thống có lỗi gì ko trước khi lên production hoàn toàn</div><h2>Cau hoi 2</h2><div class="qtext">What is the main difference between verification and validation?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Verification ensures that the software behaves as expected in real-world scenarios, while validation checks for coding standards. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Verification involves dynamic testing, while validation is purely documentation-based.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Verification checks whether the product is being built correctly, while validation checks whether the right product is being built. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. There is no difference; both terms refer to executing the code to find defects.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 3</h2><div class="qtext">Which statement about verification and validation is correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Both are only performed during testing phases. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Verification confirms the software meets design specifications, Validation confirms the software fitness for use [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Validation is part of design; verification is part of acceptance testing</div><div class="opt ">d. Verification is always automated, while validation is always manual.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.1.1 phân biệt 2 định nghĩa này như trong sách Verification = conformance to specs; Validation = fitness for purpose.</div><h2>Cau hoi 4</h2><div class="qtext">What is the correct role of test automation in software testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. To completely replace all manual testing activities [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. To find all defects in the software automatically</div><div class="opt correct">c. To support manual testing by executing repetitive and regression tests efficiently [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. To allow developers to skip writing unit tests</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 6.2 phần benefit of automation. Chọn C vì nó giúp giảm các công việc lặp lại (repetitive) ví dụ như regression test</div><h2>Cau hoi 5</h2><div class="qtext">Which factor of the following is LEAST likely to directly influence the selection of test cases for regression testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Impact analysis of recent changes [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Risk of failure in critical features</div><div class="opt correct">c. Tester’s individual skill level [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Previous defect-prone areas</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2.3 Regression test và 2.3 Maintenance test. Nhân tố nào ít ảnh hưởng nhất đến việc chọn test case cho Regression test? chọn C ( kỹ năng của 1 cá nhân ko dùng để lựa chọn TC, nó chỉ ảnh hưởng đến năng suất và chất lượng của test))</div><h2>Cau hoi 6</h2><div class="qtext">Which importance factor of a tester should be selected for regression testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Recent code changes and scope of system [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Areas with a high frequency of defects</div><div class="opt correct">c. The skill and experience of the tester performing the regression test [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Critical business functions</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.3 nhân tố Tester cần xem xét khi chọn TC cho Regression test là A. size of change và size of software, B. là mật độ lỗi cao, D là risk của tính năng nghiêm trọng đều là các nhân tố ảnh hưởng đến scope của regression test, câu hỏi đang hỏi tester chọn TC dựa vào cái gì nên chọn C dựa vào skill và experience</div><h2>Cau hoi 7</h2><div class="qtext">You need to test the login page of a web site. The page contains fields for user name and password. Which test design techniques are most appropriate for this case?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Decision coverage, fault attack [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Decision table testing, state transition testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Exploratory testing, statement coverage.</div><div class="opt ">d. Equivalence partitioning. Boundary value analysis.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.1. Kỹ thuật để test tính năng Login có combination của user và password thì tốt nhất là Decision table và kết hợp thêm State Transition testing</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements BEST describes how system complexity can create challenges when testing an AI-based system?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Testing for bias may require data that the team does not have [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Manual generation of white-box tests can be difficult [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Determining whether a system is ethical can be subjective</div><div class="opt ">d. It can be difficult to find representative data to train a model</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer câu 28 của đề AI testing họ chọn B và giải thích như sau. A sai vì Bias ( quen thuộc) test các cái quen thuộc ko dùng cho hệ thống phức tạp. C loại vì từ Ethical ( Đạo đức của hệ thống đc đánh giá chủ quan). D loại vì Train a model ko phải là công việc của test</div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">Which factor should a tester consider when selecting test cases for regression testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test case execution time [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Regression test scope [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Development budget</div><div class="opt ">d. Number of executed test cases</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.3 Chọn test case cho regression test dựa vào scope của nó</div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements about Experience Based Techniques (EBT) is correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. EBT require broad and deep knowledge in testing but not necessarily in the application or technological domain [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. EBT is based on the ability of the test engineer to implement various testing techniques.</div><div class="opt correct">c. EBT use tests derived from the test engineers' previous experience with similar technologies. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. EBT is done as a second stage of testing, after non-experienced-based testing took place.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">An input screen accepts 3 inputs; each of these has 3 equivalence classes. How many test cases are required for testing all combinations of equivalence classes?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. 3 [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. 6</div><div class="opt ">c. 9</div><div class="opt ">d. Can’t be determined</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">You have been asked to improve the way test automation tools are being used in your company. Which one of the following is the BEST approach?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Selecting and automating scripts that test new functionality to find the most defects. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Using a keyword-driven testing approach to separate the actions and data from the tool's script.</div><div class="opt ">c. Ensuring that all data, inputs and actions are stored in the tool's script for ease of maintenance</div><div class="opt ">d. Keeping expected results separate from the automation tool to allow the testers to check the results</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following answers would you expect to best describe the residual risks associated with the identified product risks, at the end of the first week of test execution?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Since R3 is the only risk for which all test cases have passed, the risk has been reduced by 20% [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. The test execution status table indicates that the risk has been reduced by 56%</div><div class="opt ">c. The residual risk level can't be determined, because it requires that all the test cases have been executed</div><div class="opt correct">d. The test execution table doesn't give an indication of the risk level of the open defects and the test cases that failed or are not run yet [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">What is the main purpose of the Three Amigos approach in Agile?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. To improve release approval process [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. To create a shared understanding of requirements and acceptance criteria [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. To measurement test coverage of system</div><div class="opt ">d. To replace the Sprint Review meeting</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.5 phần Collaborative writing user story, và đây là giải thích của từ Three amigo = collaborative: In Agile software development, the term "Three Amigos" refers to a collaborative practice, Three amigos include: Business, Development, Testing</div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">In Agile, which practice helps ensure a shared understanding of requirements?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Sprint planning [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Three Amigos [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Daily Scrum</div><div class="opt ">d. Sprint Retrospective</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.5 phần Collaborative writing user story, và đây là giải thích của từ Three amigo = collaborative: In Agile software development, the term "Three Amigos" refers to a collaborative practice, Three amigos include: Business, Development, Testing</div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">Which TWO of the following statements provide the BEST rationale for using exploratory testing?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Testers have not been allocated enough time for test design and test execution [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">b. The existing test strategy requires that testers use formal, black-box test techniques [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">c. The specification is written in a formal language that can be processed by a tool</div><div class="opt ">d. Testers are the members of an agile team and have good programming skills</div><div class="opt correct">e. Testers are experienced in the business domain and have good analytical skills [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3.2 exploratory testing hữu ích trong các trường hợp Time pressure, experienced tester</div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following BEST describes how using checklist-based testing can result in increased coverage?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Checklist items can be defined at a sufficiently low level of detail, so the tester can implement and execute detailed test cases based on these items [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Checklists can be automated, so each time an automated test execution covers the checklist items, it results in additional coverage</div><div class="opt ">c. Each checklist item should be tested separately and independently, so the elements cover different areas of the software</div><div class="opt correct">d. Two testers designing and executing tests based on the same high-level checklist items will typically perform the testing in slightly different ways [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3.3 Checklist. Dựa vào từ "high-level checklist items" là đùng định nghĩa về checklist như trong sách nhất, còn A sai vì "low level of detail", B. sai vì "Checklists can be automated" câu hỏi trong checklist thường chung chung ko thể auto đc, Còn C thì "separately and independently" cái này đang nói về định nghĩa của Unit test</div><h2>Cau hoi 18</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following best describes the purpose of the 'Three Amigos' meeting in Agile?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. To assign tasks to developers for the next sprint [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. To conduct a detailed code review before deployment</div><div class="opt correct">c. To ensure a shared understanding of a user story by discussing it from business, development, and testing perspectives [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. To review the sprint backlog and calculate team velocity</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.5 phần Collaborative writing user story, và đây là giải thích của từ Three amigo = collaborative: In Agile software development, the term "Three Amigos" refers to a collaborative practice, Three amigos include: Business, Development, Testing</div><h2>Cau hoi 19</h2><div class="qtext">For a system with complex internal code paths and conditional logic, which two techniques would be best combined?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Equivalence Partitioning and Boundary Value Analysis [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Statement Coverage and Path Coverage</div><div class="opt correct">c. Decision Table Testing and Statement Coverage [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. State Transition and Boundary Value Analysis</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.1 và 4.2. Kỹ thuật nào nên chọn cho dự án phức tạp cả về code paths và các điều kiện logic nên ta chọn cả white box test và black box test chọn C</div><h2>Cau hoi 20</h2><div class="qtext">Which standard BEST describes the classification of software failure conditions into levels such as: Catastrophic – Failure may cause a loss of life. Error or loss of critical function required to safely fly and land aircraft. Hazardous – Failure has a large negative impact on safety or performance, or reduces the ability of the crew to operate the aircraft due to physical distress or a higher workload, or causes serious injuries among the passengers. Major – Failure is significant, but has a lesser impact than a hazardous failure or significantly increases crew workload (safety related) Minor – Failure is noticeable, but has a lesser impact than a major failure. No effect – Failure has no impact on safety, aircraft operation, or crew workload.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. ISO/IEC 9126 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. IEEE 829</div><div class="opt correct">c. DO-178C [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. ISO/IEC 25010</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3 White box test</div><h2>Cau hoi 21</h2><div class="qtext">Which model emphasizes that each development phase has a corresponding testing phase, and testing is planned early in the life cycle?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Waterfall [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. V‑Model [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Scrum</div><div class="opt ">d. Regressive</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1</div><h2>Cau hoi 22</h2><div class="qtext">Which testing role is most suitable for supporting a post-release scenario where the organization aims to reduce release frequency, and gain insights from the production system?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test Manager [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Maintenance Tester [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Automation Engineer</div><div class="opt ">d. Performance Tester</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.4 Maintenance test, Vài trò của test nào phù hợp sau release? Sau release là giai đoạn maintenance cần test cho phần thay đổi và regression test nên chọn B</div><h2>Cau hoi 23</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following activities BEST reflects the contribution of a Tester in a post-release testing scenario?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Reducing Release Frequency [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Providing Insight from Production [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Blocking Exploratory Testing</div><div class="opt ">d. Prioritizing UI enhancements</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.4 Maintenance test Chọn B vì phù hợp sau release là quá trình hỗ trợ cho production</div><h2>Cau hoi 24</h2><div class="qtext">Which test technique involves learning the system, designing tests, and executing tests all at the same time?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Error guessing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Exploratory testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Faul attack</div><div class="opt ">d. Data flow based testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3 Test khám phá là cùng lúc thực hiện learn, design, execute, log</div><h2>Cau hoi 25</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following best describes a characteristic of exploratory testing in CTFL 4.1?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test cases are fully documented before test execution. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Tests are executed exactly as designed, with no deviation.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Learning, test design, and test execution occur at the same time. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. It requires detailed specifications before starting testing.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3</div><h2>Cau hoi 26</h2><div class="qtext">According to CTFL 4.1, how is test automation typically viewed within a DevOps pipeline?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. As a blocker to testing activities [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. As a quality earlier and part of the continuous feedback loop [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. As a potential security risk that should be avoided</div><div class="opt ">d. As a replacement for all manual testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1 Câu hỏi Về quy trình DevOps nói chung là test sớm và phản hồi liên tục</div><h2>Cau hoi 27</h2><div class="qtext">What is the primary purpose of MC/DC in software testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. To ensure all statements are executed at least once [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. To ensure every decision in the program has been evaluated to both true and false</div><div class="opt correct">c. To ensure each condition within a decision independently affects the outcome of the decision [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. To ensure every possible combination of conditions in a decision is tested</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 28</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following best describes the criteria for MC/DC?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Each condition within a decision independently affects the decision’s outcome, requiring that all conditions be tested in combination with others. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Each condition within a decision takes on all possible values at least once, and each decision takes on all possible outcomes at least once.</div><div class="opt ">c. All possible combinations of conditions within a decision must be tested.</div><div class="opt ">d. Every statement in the code must be executed at least once.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div></body></html>